[center][size=6][b]UE4SS for Spyro Reignited Trilogy[/b][/size]
[size=3]The UE4SS mod loader, repackaged to drop straight into Spyro Reignited Trilogy and already set to the game's engine version. This is what runs Lua mods such as [b]High FPS Gameplay Fixes[/b]. On its own it changes nothing about the game.[/size][/center]
[line]
[size=5][b]This is not my work[/b][/size]
[b]UE4SS is made by the UE4SS team[/b] (Narknon and contributors) and released under the [b]MIT License[/b], which allows anyone to redistribute it. All I did was repackage their release so it extracts into the game folder in one step, and set the engine version for this game.
[list]
[*]Original project: [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS]github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS[/url][/*]
[*]Documentation: [url=https://docs.ue4ss.com]docs.ue4ss.com[/url][/*]
[*]License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Narknon. The full text ships in the zip as [b]LICENSE.txt[/b] and installs as [b]ue4ss\LICENSE[/b].[/*]
[/list]
Please send UE4SS bugs and questions to the UE4SS project, not to this page. Problems with the packaging itself are welcome in the Posts tab.
[line]
[size=5][b]Why this page exists[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The UE4SS release page offers several files per build, and the ones starting with [b]zDEV[/b] or [b]zCustomGameConfigs[/b] are not what you want.[/*]
[*]The older [b]stable v3.0.1[/b] release does not work with some Spyro mods, including High FPS Gameplay Fixes. You need an [b]experimental[/b] build.[/*]
[*]UE4SS has to know the engine version. Spyro Reignited Trilogy is Unreal Engine [b]4.19[/b], and that is already filled in here.[/*]
[*]The official zip extracts into [b]Falcon\Binaries\Win64[/b], while Spyro mod zips extract into the [b]game folder[/b]. This one uses the game folder too, so both are installed the same way.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b]What is in the download[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]UE4SS [b]{{UE4SS_VERSION}}[/b] (experimental), exactly as released, including the UE4SS mods that come with it (console, Blueprint mod loader and so on).[/*]
[*]One change: [b]UE4SS-settings.ini[/b] has the engine version set to [b]4.19[/b]. Nothing else is modified.[/*]
[*]The MIT license text and a readme with these instructions.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]1. Find the game folder[/b]
In Steam, right-click [b]Spyro Reignited Trilogy[/b] → [b]Manage[/b] → [b]Browse local files[/b]. Usually:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Spyro Reignited Trilogy[/code]
[b]2. Extract the zip into that folder[/b]
Not into Win64: the zip already contains the right folders. Afterwards you have:
[code]Spyro Reignited Trilogy\Falcon\Binaries\Win64\dwmapi.dll
Spyro Reignited Trilogy\Falcon\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\[/code]
[b]dwmapi.dll[/b] must sit directly next to [b]Spyro-Win64-Shipping.exe[/b]. If Windows asks whether to merge folders, choose Yes.
[b]3. [color=#3d85c6]LINUX, STEAM DECK AND PROTON ONLY[/color][/b]
Add this to the game's Steam launch options:
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dwmapi.dll=n,b" %command%[/code]
[b]4. Check that it works[/b]
Start the game. Nothing appears on screen; that is normal. This file should now exist:
[code]Spyro Reignited Trilogy\Falcon\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\UE4SS.log[/code]
[line]
[size=5][b]Installing mods with it[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Lua mods[/b] are folders under [b]Falcon\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\[/b] containing [b]Scripts\main.lua[/b] and an empty file named [b]enabled.txt[/b]. Most mod zips already have that layout, so you extract them into the game folder just like this one.[/*]
[*][b]Restart the game[/b] after adding or changing mods. UE4SS's hot reload (Ctrl+R) can crash Spyro.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]No UE4SS.log appears:[/b] check that [b]dwmapi.dll[/b] is directly next to [b]Spyro-Win64-Shipping.exe[/b] and not inside the ue4ss folder. Some antivirus programs quarantine it, so check your antivirus history and restore it if needed.[/*]
[*][b]A mod says it needs a newer UE4SS than stable v3.0.1:[/b] this download is that newer build.[/*]
[*][b]Want to see the UE4SS log window while you play?[/b] Set [b]ConsoleEnabled = 1[/b] in [b]Falcon\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\UE4SS-settings.ini[/b].[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [b]dwmapi.dll[/b] and the [b]ue4ss[/b] folder from [b]Falcon\Binaries\Win64[/b]. That removes the log with it. Lua mods you installed live inside the ue4ss folder and go too.
[line]
